|May 11th, 12:50 GMT
|Clue Scrolls added to the Hallowed Sepulchre are replacing existing rolls and they are not an additional roll on the drop table.

The Poll 76 blog did not specify that they would replace rolls, so players feel confused because they expected Clue Scrolls to be in addition to the loot you currently receive.
|The Poll 76 blog did not specify exactly how the rolls would work, however, typically in the past we have added clues as an additional roll on the droptable. The Hallowed Sepulchre already had a very strong drop table and we didn't want it to become too powerful, which is why a decision was made during development to have them replace existing rolls.

We do not want players to feel mislead by the original blog as we know this may have influenced the way it was voted on. Moving forward, we'll try to be more explicit about these considerations in poll blogs wherever possible. Certain decisions (such as in this case) need to be made in development for balancing reasons. For now, we'd like to hear your feedback on it and we will review whether this needs to be changed following more feedback. Please let us know what you think and we will take this into consideration.

'''Update - 13:45 BST, May 12th''' We have implemented a hotfix to make the Clue Scroll drops to be tertiary rolls, rather than replacing rolls.
|-
|May 11th, 16:00 BST
|Clue Scrolls from the Hallowed Sepulchre had only one step.
|'''HOTFIXED - 16:00 BST''' Clue Scrolls will henceforth have an appropriate number of steps, as is normal for their tier.
